            "description": "Watch Flamengo vs Cusco highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 26, 2026. Flamengo and Cusco faced off in a highly anticipated CONMEBOL Libertadores fixture on May 26, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as both teams sought to establish dominance in one of South America's most prestigious football competitions. A Gritty Battle in the Opening Half The match began with a display of tactical discipline and physical intensity. Cusco set up a resilient defensive block that frustrated Flamengo 's creative outlets early on. The competitive nature of the game was evident as the referee stayed busy, issuing yellow cards to Diego Soto in the 14th minute and Gabriel Carabajal in the 31st. Despite controlling much of the possession, the home side struggled to find a clinical finish, and the first half concluded without a goal, leaving the fans in suspense. Tactical Shifts and Sustained Pressure As the second half got underway, both managers turned to their benches to find a spark. Cusco introduced Oswaldo Valenzuela and Juan Manuel Tevez , but their disciplinary struggles continued with Tevez and Carlos Diez also entering the referee's book. Flamengo responded by bringing on heavyweight reinforcements; the introduction of Pedro and Erick Pulgar at the hour mark, followed by Lucas Paquetá shortly after, shifted the momentum firmly in favor of the Brazilian giants. Bruno Henrique Leads the Late Charge The deadlock was finally broken in the 80th minute when Pedro turned provider, setting up Bruno Henrique for a clinical strike. The goal opened the floodgates, and the Cusco defense, which had been so sturdy for over an hour, began to crumble. Just four minutes later, Bruno Henrique struck again, doubling the lead and effectively putting the game out of reach for the visitors. In the dying moments, the drama continued as Alvaro Ampuero was cautioned for a foul in the box in the 89th minute. Lucas Paquetá stepped up to the spot and calmly converted the penalty in the first minute of stoppage time. The 3-0 result capped off a professional performance by Flamengo , who displayed patience and clinical finishing to secure all three points.",
